{
  "id": "a1-g03",
  "slides": [
    {
      "type": "cover",
      "title": "The verb to be",
      "subtitle": "Verbo *to be* en presente: afirmativa, negativa y preguntas",
      "goals": [
        "Usar **am, is, are** con cada pronombre.",
        "Formar oraciones **negativas** y **preguntas**.",
        "Responder con **respuestas cortas**: *Yes, I am. / No, she isn't.*"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "explain",
      "title": "Afirmativa: am, is, are",
      "body": [
        "*To be* equivale a **ser** y **estar**. En la conversación casi siempre se usa la **contracción**."
      ],
      "table": {
        "head": ["Forma completa", "Contracción", "Escucha"],
        "rows": [
          ["I **am**", "I'm", "I'm"],
          ["you **are**", "you're", "you're"],
          ["he **is**", "he's", "he's"],
          ["she **is**", "she's", "she's"],
          ["it **is**", "it's", "it's"],
          ["we **are**", "we're", "we're"],
          ["they **are**", "they're", "they're"]
        ],
        "speak": 2
      },
      "list": [
        "Origen: *I'm from Mexico.*",
        "Profesión, con **a / an**: *She's **a** doctor.*",
        "Edad: *I'm 19 years old.*",
        "Estados y sensaciones: *We're tired. Are you hungry?*",
        "Lugar: *They're at school.*"
      ],
      "errors": [
        { "bad": "I have 19 years.", "good": "I **am** 19 years old.", "note": "La edad se dice con **to be**, no con *have*." },
        { "bad": "She is doctor.", "good": "She is **a** doctor.", "note": "Las profesiones en singular llevan **a / an**." }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "examples",
      "title": "To be en la vida diaria",
      "items": [
        { "en": "I'm Mel. I'm a teacher.", "es": "Soy Mel. Soy maestra." },
        { "en": "You're in group 1A.", "es": "Estás en el grupo 1A." },
        { "en": "He's 20 years old.", "es": "Tiene 20 años." },
        { "en": "It's a great app.", "es": "Es una gran app." },
        { "en": "We're from Santa Rosa Jáuregui.", "say": "We're from Santa Rosa.", "es": "Somos de Santa Rosa Jáuregui." },
        { "en": "They're hungry.", "es": "Tienen hambre.", "note": "*hungry, thirsty, cold, hot* van con **to be**." }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "fill",
      "title": "Completa con am, is o are",
      "items": [
        { "t": "I ___ a student.", "a": ["am"] },
        { "t": "My brother ___ a mechanic.", "a": ["is"] },
        { "t": "You ___ very kind.", "a": ["are"] },
        { "t": "The classroom ___ big.", "a": ["is"] },
        { "t": "Luis and Ana ___ from Querétaro.", "a": ["are"], "why": "Dos personas → *they* → **are**." },
        { "t": "We ___ ready.", "a": ["are"] }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "explain",
      "title": "Negativa y preguntas",
      "table": {
        "head": ["", "Forma", "Ejemplo"],
        "rows": [
          ["Negativa", "sujeto + am / is / are + **not**", "She **isn't** at home. / I**'m not** tired."],
          ["Pregunta", "**Am / Is / Are** + sujeto + …?", "**Are** you a student? **Is** he your brother?"],
          ["Pregunta con *wh-*", "Wh- + am / is / are + sujeto?", "**Where are** you from? **How old is** she?"],
          ["Respuesta corta", "Yes, sujeto + verbo. / No, sujeto + verbo + not.", "Yes, I **am**. No, he **isn't**."]
        ]
      },
      "errors": [
        { "bad": "I amn't ready.", "good": "I'**m not** ready.", "note": "*Amn't* no existe en inglés estándar." },
        { "bad": "Yes, I'm.", "good": "Yes, I **am**.", "note": "En respuestas cortas **afirmativas** no se contrae." }
      ],
      "tip": "*isn't* = *is not* · *aren't* = *are not*. También se dice *she's not* y *they're not*."
    },
    {
      "type": "examples",
      "title": "Preguntas y respuestas cortas",
      "items": [
        { "en": "Are you a student? — Yes, I am.", "es": "¿Eres estudiante? — Sí." },
        { "en": "Is she your sister? — No, she isn't.", "es": "¿Es tu hermana? — No." },
        { "en": "Are they at school? — Yes, they are.", "es": "¿Están en la escuela? — Sí." },
        { "en": "Where are you from? — I'm from Mexico.", "es": "¿De dónde eres? — Soy de México." },
        { "en": "How old is he? — He's twenty-two.", "es": "¿Cuántos años tiene? — Tiene 22." }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "mc",
      "title": "Elige la forma correcta",
      "items": [
        { "q": "___ you tired?", "options": ["Is", "Are", "Am"], "a": 1 },
        { "q": "My phone ___ new.", "options": ["isn't", "aren't", "amn't"], "a": 0 },
        { "q": "¿Cómo se dice *Tengo 18 años*?", "options": ["I have 18 years.", "I am 18 years.", "I'm 18 years old."], "a": 2, "why": "La edad va con **to be**: *I'm 18 (years old)*." },
        { "q": "Is Carlos an engineer? — Yes, ___", "options": ["he's.", "he is.", "is he."], "a": 1, "why": "En respuestas cortas afirmativas no se contrae." },
        { "q": "Where ___ they from?", "options": ["is", "am", "are"], "a": 2 },
        { "q": "I ___ hungry. I just ate.", "options": ["'m not", "isn't", "aren't"], "a": 0 }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "order",
      "title": "Ordena las preguntas",
      "items": [
        { "a": "Are you a student?", "es": "¿Eres estudiante?" },
        { "a": "Is she from Mexico?", "es": "¿Ella es de México?" },
        { "a": "Where are they now?", "es": "¿Dónde están ahora?" },
        { "a": "How old is your brother?", "es": "¿Cuántos años tiene tu hermano?" }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "match",
      "title": "Relaciona la pregunta con su respuesta",
      "pairs": [
        ["Are you tired?", "Yes, I am."],
        ["Is he a teacher?", "No, he isn't."],
        ["Are they at home?", "Yes, they are."],
        ["Is it cold?", "No, it isn't."],
        ["Am I late?", "Yes, you are."],
        ["Is Ana your sister?", "Yes, she is."]
      ],
      "speak": "left"
    },
    {
      "type": "fill",
      "title": "Escribe la negativa",
      "items": [
        { "t": "He is at school. → He ___ at school.", "a": ["isn't", "is not", "'s not"] },
